body:
# Contraband Scanner - mod for Minecraft 1.21.1 (NeoForge)

Item **"Prohibited Scanner"**: by pressing RMB, it checks the area and writes to the chat,
whether a forbidden item was found (by default - items from the `nirvana` mod).

What is scanned in radius (default 50 blocks):
- containers - chests, barrels, shulkers, furnaces, hoppers, dispensers and any
mod blocks that provide a standard ItemHandler;
- blocks in the world - growing plants, cars, any blocks of the target mod;
- objects lying on the ground;
- inventories of other players and their ender chests.

Right click - detection by range zones, without exact coordinates:
- up to `detectorRadius` (16 m) - “close proximity is prohibited, aim with the detector”;
- from `detectorRadius` to `scanRadius` (16–50 m) - “prohibited nearby” (just a fact);
- from `scanRadius` to `farRadius` (50–100 m) - “there is a prohibition” + cardinal direction;
- further than `farRadius` (100 m) - it does not see.

The exact location is never given out: from afar you get directions, closer - a fact
presence, but the squeak of the detector brings it close. The pitch of the sound is higher for
near zones and lower for distant zones.

Metal detector mode: while an item is selected in the hand, it passively “rings”
area and beeps - the closer to the prohibited, the more often the squeak and the higher the tone. Right click
at the same time, it still produces a full report with a list of finds.
